Package: slrxfm
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Smech Labs Remastered Xandros File Manager
 SLRXFM is a clean-room, from-scratch reimplementation of the behavior
 of XandrosFileManager, the proprietary file manager shipped with
 Xandros Desktop 1.0 (2002), part of a broader historical-preservation
 and software-recreation project for that distribution. No original
 Xandros code, decompiled or otherwise, is present in this package;
 see /usr/share/doc/slrxfm/CLEAN_ROOM.md for the methodology.
 .
 It provides a folder tree and file-detail listing, with copy, cut,
 paste, delete, and rename; move-to-trash, restore, and empty-trash;
 symlink creation; and browsing of local, SMB, FTP, and WebDAV
 locations through one unified interface.
